---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Code Signing Policy"
  description="Code signing policy for Pits n' Giggles: what is signed, who signs it, and how to verify a download."
>
  <div class="pt-32 pb-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto prose prose-invert prose-lg">
        <h1>Code Signing Policy</h1>

        <div class="bg-green-900/20 border border-green-700 rounded-lg p-6 mb-8">
          <p class="mb-0">
            Free code signing provided by <a href="https://signpath.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SignPath.io</a>,
            certificate by <a href="https://signpath.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SignPath Foundation</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>What is signed</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The Windows release EXE on the
            <a href="https://github.com/ashwin-nat/pits-n-giggles/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Releases page</a>,
            starting with the first release after the production certificate is issued (version to be announced here).
            Older releases are unsigned.
          </li>
          <li>
            It is built from the public repository by GitHub Actions. SignPath checks that each signing request comes from
            that repository's own build, and every release is approved by hand before it is signed.
          </li>
          <li>macOS builds are not signed.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How to check a download</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Right-click the EXE, choose Properties, then <strong>Digital Signatures</strong>. The signer should be <em>SignPath Foundation</em>.</li>
          <li>Compare the file's SHA256 against <code>checksums.txt</code> on the same release.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Team roles</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Committers and reviewers: <a href="https://github.com/ashwin-nat" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ashwin-nat</a></li>
          <li>Approvers: <a href="https://github.com/ashwin-nat" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ashwin-nat</a></li>
          <li>Outside contributions come in as pull requests and are reviewed before merge.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The app collects no personal data. The only outside requests are the launcher's anonymous version check to GitHub
          and, in Time Trial sessions, a pole-lap lookup to OpenF1. Details are in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
        <p>
          If a signed file looks wrong or a signature doesn't verify, please open an issue on
          <a href="https://github.com/ashwin-nat/pits-n-giggles/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Issues</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
